The card's three must-allows are tests and hold (a success shows nothing, no deploy yet shows nothing, a later success clears a failure). Two guards the tests name are not held by them.

F1 (MEDIUM, escaping): the chip's visible reason is not tested escaped. Mutant: in worker/page-header.mjs, <span class="detail">${esc(dfail)}</span> -> ${dfail} survives the touched tests. The test's html("<img src=x>") check matches the title attribute's &lt;img, which is still escaped, so the visible span can carry raw markup. The store's shape (deploy-last-shape) admits any printable ASCII, < and > included. Fix: assert the detail span itself, e.g. that html("<img src=x>") has no "<img" anywhere and has <span class="detail">&lt;img src=x&gt;</span>.

F2 (LOW, vacuous test): "the deploy run records its failure with the token taken out" never has a token to take out. Mutant: recordLast(..., line: redact(why, creds)) -> line: why survives. In the test the private file read throws, so creds is null and redact does nothing either way; the test asserts only /dirty/. Fix: give the run creds (a board.private.json with a token and account) and a failing step whose output holds both; assert neither is in board-deploy-last.json.

